<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rrn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The UPI retrieval reference number of a payment."@en .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rrn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "RRN"@en .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rrn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-10> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#Rule> .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-10> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "One bill, one payment. Every UPI request carries the bill ID, and a debit with no approved payment is a customer charged twice until proven otherwise."@en .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-10> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rule 10"@en .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-10> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#governs> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#Debit> .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-10> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#governs> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#PaymentAttempt> .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-10> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#solves> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#kpi-charged-twice> .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-10> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#solves> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#kpi-match-rate> .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-11> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#Rule> .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-11> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A refund answers a debit. The clock starts at the extra debit, not at the complaint."@en .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-11> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rule 11"@en .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-11> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#governs> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#Refund> .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-11> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#solves> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#kpi-refund-tat> .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-12> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#Rule> .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-12> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Every record either looks at the world or copies another record. Before acting on a KPI, find the record it reads and an observation that can contradict it."@en .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-12> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rule 12"@en .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-12> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#governs> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#Record> .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#Rule> .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Available means on the shelf. Book stock is a belief – the last count, plus receipts, minus sales and write-offs."@en .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rule 1"@en .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-1> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#governs> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#Stock> .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-1> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#solves> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#kpi-days-of-supply> .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-1> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#solves> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#kpi-ira> .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-1> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#solves> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#kpi-osa> .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#Rule> .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Silence is a question. No sales while the books show stock means someone should look at the shelf."@en .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rule 2"@en .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-2> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#governs> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#LostSale> .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-2> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#governs> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#Stock> .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-2> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#solves> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#kpi-ira> .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-2> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#solves> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#kpi-lost-sales> .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-2> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#solves> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#kpi-osa> .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#Rule> .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Demand is not sales. Demand that finds an empty shelf becomes a lost sale, which no record holds – estimate it and say how."@en .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rule 3"@en .
<https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#rule-3> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#governs> <https://kvinayakpai.github.io/domain-series/ontology/store-014#Demand> .
